ace in 07:12:56, followed by Jenny WILSON (07:23:45).\n\nBruce FORDYCE's 05:30:12 broke FORDYCE's own up record of 05:37:28 set in 1981. Lindsay WEIGHT's 07:12:56 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1948 (Bill Savage, 07:13:52).\n\nFrom a field of 5,365 entries, 5,363 runners completed the course for a 100.0% finish rate. The field comprised 5,203 men and 160 women (3.0% female). The average finish time was 09:14:30.\n\nMedals awarded: 11 Gold, 582 Silver, 4,770 Bronze. 1,873 runners (34.9%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Martin THERON in 10:59:59.\n\nCompared to the previous up run in 1981, the field was 46.5% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 24% of the finishers, with 4,062 seniors (avg 09:10:51) and 1,299 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":0.0}